{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"misandrous-panpsychic-armadillo","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n2026-11-04 PST, worktree fix-jaeger at commit d413a0497e5 (bug bronze-commonable-jaeger, MCP auth wiring only). The integration tier as `make test` runs it (`pytest -m integration -n 4 --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0 -q`) reported `1 failed, 201 passed, 3 skipped in 736.10s`. The failure was not an assertion: xdist worker gw2 terminated abnormally (\"node down: Not properly terminated\"; the rebar crash guard reported it) while running `tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass`. The tier normally takes about 3 min 40 s; this run took 12 min 16 s.\n\nHost state shortly after: load average about 28-33 on 18 cores, `memory_pressure` reporting 14% free.\n\nIsolated reruns on the same tree all passed, but each took 204-297 s (3 runs: 250.8 s, 204.6 s, 297.5 s).\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\n- The worker process was killed under memory pressure (for example by the OS) while this long-running benchmark held a large working set.\n- The benchmark's runtime under load crossed a worker-level limit that ends the process abnormally.\n- Another defect in the test or the import batch path that only shows under parallel load.\n\n## Next check\n\nRerun the integration tier with per-worker peak RSS recorded, and check the macOS unified log for a jetsam/kill event for the worker pid at the crash time. A kill event would point at memory; no kill plus a stack would point at the test itself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause identified with evidence recorded as a ticket comment.\n- [ ] `pytest -m integration -n 4 --dist loadgroup --max-worker-restart=0 -q` completes with no worker crash in this test on a loaded host, or the class of failure is fixed with a regression test.","id":"9580-52b1-252f-46eb","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Integration worker crashes in test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass under load"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793798658958545001,"uuid":"d70daf54-ed7e-4f69-b24c-23e6812e2a20"}